{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"fe84fcd785b0c2af8cb09678","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987%40gmail.com/","channels":["lkml","platform-driver-x86"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987@gmail.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] platform/x86: asus-armoury: add support for FX517ZR","messages":{"9cb5f4f9-223f-4162-8b9a-81486944be54@linux.dev":{"id":"9cb5f4f9-223f-4162-8b9a-81486944be54@linux.dev","messageId":"9cb5f4f9-223f-4162-8b9a-81486944be54@linux.dev","references":["20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987@gmail.com"],"author":{"name":"Denis Benato","address":"denis.benato@linux.dev"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"AbdElRahman Soliman","address":"abdelrahman7987@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"hansg@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"ilpo.jarvinen@linux.intel.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"platform-driver-x86@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T14:48:59.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T14:48:59.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] platform/x86: asus-armoury: add support for FX517ZR","mailingLists":[{"id":"platform-driver-x86.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"platform-driver-x86.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 7/29/26 13:09, AbdElRahman Soliman wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Add DMI match and power-limit table entry for the ASUS TUF Dash F15"},{"depth":1,"text":"(2022), board FX517ZR, an Alder Lake + RTX 3070 laptop."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"AC and DC min/max values for ppt_pl1_spl, ppt_pl2_sppt,"},{"depth":1,"text":"nv_dynamic_boost and nv_temp_target were read from the sliders in"},{"depth":1,"text":"ASUS Armoury Crate's manual performance-tuning mode on Windows for"},{"depth":1,"text":"this exact model, since ASUS does not publish these limits on the Web."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Tested locally: values now report correctly via 'asusctl armoury"},{"depth":1,"text":"list' instead of unavailable, and Dynamic Boost via nvidia-powerd"},{"depth":1,"text":"measurably raises GPU power limit under load, consistent with the"},{"depth":1,"text":"80W base + 25W boost = 105W max TGP in ASUS's own spec sheet for"},{"depth":1,"text":"this configuration."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5"}],"lineCount":15,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks for this."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I would say remove the \"Tested locally\" paragraph: guidelines says\nthat commit messages are to be written in the second person as if\nyou were telling git what to do."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Also I personally never used a commit message so long and\na shorter one will be absolutely be fine too."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Next revision use the -v2 flag and don't forget to email me too."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"If you need further help just tell me, thanks!"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: AbdElRahman Soliman <abdelrahman7987@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/platform/x86/asus-armoury.h | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-armoury.h b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-armoury.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"index bc899bec7..46c308ba8 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-armoury.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-armoury.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -975,6 +975,32 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id power_limits[] = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t.requires_fan_curve = true,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t},"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t.matches = {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tDMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, \"FX517ZR\"),"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t.driver_data = &(struct power_data) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t.ac_data = &(struct power_limits) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl1_spl_min = 28,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl1_spl_max = 85,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl2_sppt_min = 28,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl2_sppt_max = 135,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_dynamic_boost_min = 5,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_dynamic_boost_max = 25,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_temp_target_min = 75,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_temp_target_max = 87,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t.dc_data = &(struct power_limits) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl1_spl_min = 25,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl1_spl_max = 45,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl2_sppt_min = 35,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.ppt_pl2_sppt_max = 60,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_temp_target_min = 75,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t.nv_temp_target_max = 87,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t.requires_fan_curve = true,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t{"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t.matches = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tDMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, \"FX607VU\"),"}],"lineCount":42,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260729110941.26794-1-abdelrahman7987@gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["9cb5f4f9-223f-4162-8b9a-81486944be54@linux.dev"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["9cb5f4f9-223f-4162-8b9a-81486944be54@linux.dev"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}